WEBVTT

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:05.600
Welcome to Attention Lab. This is Day One:
find a workable seat.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:08.495
This guide contains a five minute
practice, plus this introduction and a

00:00:08.495 --> 00:00:11.390
short closing.

00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:15.510
You are practicing choosing attention,
recognizing wandering, and returning. A
quiet mind

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:19.630
is not required.

00:00:26.034 --> 00:00:29.638
Choose a safe place to sit. A chair is
enough. Keep your

00:00:29.638 --> 00:00:33.244
eyes open or close them if comfortable.

00:00:33.244 --> 00:00:36.328
Let breathing remain ordinary. You do not
need to hold, deepen, or

00:00:36.328 --> 00:00:39.414
slow it.

00:00:39.414 --> 00:00:42.598
Adjust your posture or stop whenever
needed. The gentle bell marks each

00:00:42.598 --> 00:00:45.784
change of task.

00:00:52.222 --> 00:00:55.867
Imagine carefully counting five hundred
rupee notes when a mistake could cost

00:00:55.867 --> 00:00:59.512
you money. Attention would likely become
more precise because the task feels

00:00:59.512 --> 00:01:03.157
important.

00:01:03.157 --> 00:01:08.970
This suggests that motivation and
perceived importance can affect attention.
Struggling to

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:14.782
focus during meditation does not
necessarily mean you lack attentional
capacity.

00:01:14.782 --> 00:01:18.445
We will not create financial anxiety or
penalties. Our purpose is simply

00:01:18.445 --> 00:01:22.109
to practice one useful return. This is an
analogy, not a special

00:01:22.109 --> 00:01:25.772
technique.

00:01:34.106 --> 00:01:37.826
First timebox. One minute to settle the
body.

00:01:37.826 --> 00:01:41.663
Sit with your feet or legs supported, and
let your hands rest.

00:01:41.663 --> 00:01:45.500
Let your back be upright without bracing.

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:49.070
Feel the support of the seat. Soften easy
tension in the jaw,

00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:52.640
shoulders, and hands.

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:55.878
If attention wanders, feel one contact
point again. Adjust your position whenever

00:01:55.878 --> 00:01:59.116
needed.

00:02:34.066 --> 00:02:37.896
Second timebox. Two minutes to feel the
support.

00:02:37.896 --> 00:02:41.320
Notice both feet and the seat. Choose one
contact point and observe

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:44.746
the pressure there. Keep breathing
natural.

00:02:44.746 --> 00:02:49.080
Notice whether the pressure stays similar
or changes slightly. There is no

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:53.416
need to make it different.

00:02:53.416 --> 00:02:56.520
If a thought draws you away, recognize
that shift and feel the

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:59.626
same contact point again.

00:02:59.626 --> 00:03:02.796
Continue with this one task until the next
bell.

00:04:34.056 --> 00:04:38.540
Third timebox. One minute to practice a
deliberate return.

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:42.733
Observe feet or hand contact. When a
thought draws attention away, recognize

00:04:42.733 --> 00:04:46.926
that shift and feel contact again.

00:04:46.926 --> 00:04:49.203
You do not need to argue with the thought
or begin the

00:04:49.203 --> 00:04:51.480
whole session again.

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:54.633
Each recognition gives you another
opportunity to return. Continue this small
task

00:04:54.633 --> 00:04:57.786
until the bell.

00:05:34.085 --> 00:05:38.105
Final timebox. One minute to close without
grading.

00:05:38.106 --> 00:05:41.563
Keep one body contact point clear. Release
extra commentary about whether this

00:05:41.563 --> 00:05:45.020
session was good enough.

00:05:45.020 --> 00:05:49.380
If you wander into evaluation, feel your
feet or hands again.

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:52.628
You are training a skill. Calm, silence,
or a special experience is

00:05:52.628 --> 00:05:55.876
not required.

00:06:34.106 --> 00:06:38.118
The five minute practice is complete. Open
your eyes if closed, feel

00:06:38.118 --> 00:06:42.130
your support, and look around before
standing.

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:46.145
For your reflection, name one contact
point you returned to. What helped

00:06:46.145 --> 00:06:50.160
you feel supported rather than rigid?

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:53.993
A useful beginning can be one clear
recognition and one deliberate return.

00:06:53.993 --> 00:06:57.826
Continue at a pace you can sustain.

